# SmritiSetu Dashboard (Developer 3)

You own **smritisetu-dashboard** only — caregiver & healthcare-worker web UI. Do not generate backend or patient mobile app code. Consume documented API contracts; mock until OpenAPI ships.

## Non-negotiable product rule

This system supports care. It never diagnoses, treats, or claims to cure dementia.

- Never display a single dementia/risk score.
- Never phrase UI as diagnosis or medical certainty.
- Prefer plain-language observations (e.g. "Participation decreased over seven days.").
- Label every note with author role: system, caregiver, healthcare worker, or clinician.
- Red/urgent styling only for genuinely urgent action items.
- Show non-diagnostic disclaimer near trends/charts/export.
- Reminder states are acknowledgements/misses — never claim medicine was taken.

## Stack (fixed)

Next.js + TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS, Recharts, JWT auth (`/auth/login`, `/auth/refresh`, `/devices/pair`).

## Structure

- Screens by route; shared UI in `components/ui`
- API in `lib/api/` — swap mocks for live via env, one-file change
- Every screen: loading, empty, offline, permission-denied, error states

## Contract gaps

Flag missing endpoints in `CONTRACT_GAPS.md`. Do not invent fields outside the shared data model without flagging. `POST /devices/pair` is documented — not a gap.
